    "content": "<div class=\"ml-en\"><span class=\"eyebrow\">MCO302 · Chapter 6 · Session 19</span>\n<h2>Session 19 — Chapter 5: Identity and Intercultural Communication (Part 4)</h2>\n<p class=\"nhan\">Source: FLM syllabus 13649 · session plan</p></div>\n<div class=\"ml-vi\"><span class=\"eyebrow\">MCO302 · Chương 6 · Buổi 19</span>\n<h2>Buổi 19 — Chapter 5: Identity and Intercultural Communication (Part 4)</h2>\n<p class=\"nhan\">Nguồn: syllabus FLM 13649 · kế hoạch buổi</p></div>\n<div class=\"ml-en\"><div class=\"kv-grid\">\n  <div class=\"kv\"><span class=\"k\">Type</span><span class=\"v\">Offline</span></div>\n  <div class=\"kv\"><span class=\"k\">LO</span><span class=\"v\">CLO1, CLO3, CLO5, CLO8</span></div>\n  <div class=\"kv\"><span class=\"k\">ITU</span><span class=\"v\">I,T</span></div>\n  <div class=\"kv\"><span class=\"k\">Slides in this lesson</span><span class=\"v\">none from FLM</span></div>\n</div></div>\n<div class=\"ml-vi\"><div class=\"kv-grid\">\n  <div class=\"kv\"><span class=\"k\">Hình thức</span><span class=\"v\">Offline</span></div>\n  <div class=\"kv\"><span class=\"k\">LO</span><span class=\"v\">CLO1, CLO3, CLO5, CLO8</span></div>\n  <div class=\"kv\"><span class=\"k\">ITU</span><span class=\"v\">I,T</span></div>\n  <div class=\"kv\"><span class=\"k\">Slide trong bài</span><span class=\"v\">FLM không có</span></div>\n</div></div>\n<div class=\"ml-en\"><h3>What this session covers (FLM, verbatim)</h3></div>\n<div class=\"ml-vi\"><h3>Nội dung buổi học (FLM, nguyên văn)</h3></div>\n<p>Chapter 5: Identity and Intercultural Communication (Part 4)<br>Identity, Stereotypes, and Prejudice<br>Classroom Activity: “AI and Cultural Stereotypes”</p>\n<div class=\"ml-en\"><h3>Materials to read</h3></div>\n<div class=\"ml-vi\"><h3>Tài liệu cần đọc</h3></div>\n<p>Textbooks<br>Any further additional reading materials if recommended by lecturer</p>\n<div class=\"ml-en\"><h3>Student's tasks</h3></div>\n<div class=\"ml-vi\"><h3>Nhiệm vụ sinh viên</h3></div>\n<p>Lecture/ Presentation<br>Q&amp;A/ Discussions<br><br>Classroom Activity: “AI and Cultural Stereotypes”<br>1. Warm-Up Discussion (5 mins):<br>Ask students: “Have you ever heard a stereotype about your culture or another culture?” Encourage examples like: “Americans are too direct,” “Japanese are overly formal,” “Vietnamese people are always late.”<br>2. AI Investigation (15–20 mins): In pairs or small groups, students choose one cultural stereotype. Using AI, they explore:<br>- What is the stereotype?<br>- Where does it come from?<br>- Is it accurate or problematic?<br>- What counterexamples or facts challenge it?<br>- How can intercultural communication overcome this stereotype?<br>Example prompt for AI: “Why do people think Vietnamese are always late? Is this stereotype accurate or harmful?”<br>3. Quick Presentation (10 mins): Each group shares:<br>- The stereotype they chose<br>- What AI revealed about it<br>- Whether they agree or disagree<br>- One strategy to challenge the stereotype in real-life communication<br>4. Individual Reflection (5 mins): Students write a short response: “One stereotype I used to believe was… After this activity, I now think…”</p>\n<div class=\"ml-en\"><h3>Constructive questions — answer them yourself first</h3></div>\n<div class=\"ml-vi\"><h3>Câu hỏi kiến tạo — tự trả lời trước</h3></div>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>QN19.1</strong> — Is there any idea that is popular in Vietnamese but you cannot express that idea in English?</li>\n</ul>\n<div class=\"ml-en\"><div class=\"note-ct\">📝 Detailed lecture and 🎬 video for this session: coming later. For now follow the slides, the materials and the tasks above.</div></div>\n<div class=\"ml-vi\"><div class=\"note-ct\">📝 Bài giảng chi tiết và 🎬 video cho buổi này: sẽ bổ sung sau. Trước mắt học theo slide, tài liệu và nhiệm vụ ở trên.</div></div>"
