    "content": "<div class=\"ml-en\"><span class=\"eyebrow\">MCO302 · Chapter 10 · Session 36</span>\n<h2>Session 36 — Chapter 9: Popular Culture and Intercultural Communication (Part 3)</h2>\n<p class=\"nhan\">Source: FLM syllabus 13649 · session plan</p></div>\n<div class=\"ml-vi\"><span class=\"eyebrow\">MCO302 · Chương 10 · Buổi 36</span>\n<h2>Buổi 36 — Chapter 9: Popular Culture and Intercultural Communication (Part 3)</h2>\n<p class=\"nhan\">Nguồn: syllabus FLM 13649 · kế hoạch buổi</p></div>\n<div class=\"ml-en\"><div class=\"kv-grid\">\n  <div class=\"kv\"><span class=\"k\">Type</span><span class=\"v\">Offline</span></div>\n  <div class=\"kv\"><span class=\"k\">LO</span><span class=\"v\">CLO1, CLO3, CLO4, CLO8</span></div>\n  <div class=\"kv\"><span class=\"k\">ITU</span><span class=\"v\">I,T</span></div>\n  <div class=\"kv\"><span class=\"k\">Slides in this lesson</span><span class=\"v\">none from FLM</span></div>\n</div></div>\n<div class=\"ml-vi\"><div class=\"kv-grid\">\n  <div class=\"kv\"><span class=\"k\">Hình thức</span><span class=\"v\">Offline</span></div>\n  <div class=\"kv\"><span class=\"k\">LO</span><span class=\"v\">CLO1, CLO3, CLO4, CLO8</span></div>\n  <div class=\"kv\"><span class=\"k\">ITU</span><span class=\"v\">I,T</span></div>\n  <div class=\"kv\"><span class=\"k\">Slide trong bài</span><span class=\"v\">FLM không có</span></div>\n</div></div>\n<div class=\"ml-en\"><h3>What this session covers (FLM, verbatim)</h3></div>\n<div class=\"ml-vi\"><h3>Nội dung buổi học (FLM, nguyên văn)</h3></div>\n<p>Chapter 9: Popular Culture and Intercultural Communication (Part 3)<br>U.S. Popular Culture and Power<br>Classroom Activity: “Decoding U.S. Pop Culture with AI”</p>\n<div class=\"ml-en\"><h3>Materials to read</h3></div>\n<div class=\"ml-vi\"><h3>Tài liệu cần đọc</h3></div>\n<p>Textbooks<br>Any further additional reading materials if recommended by lecturer</p>\n<div class=\"ml-en\"><h3>Student's tasks</h3></div>\n<div class=\"ml-vi\"><h3>Nhiệm vụ sinh viên</h3></div>\n<p>Lecture/ Presentation<br>Q&amp;A/ Discussions<br>Classroom Activity: “Decoding U.S. Pop Culture with AI”<br>1. Warm-Up Discussion (5 mins): Ask students: “What’s one American song, movie, or trend you’ve seen recently? How did it make you feel or think?” Encourage examples like Marvel movies, TikTok dances, hip-hop music, fast food brands, etc.<br>2. AI Exploration Task (15–20 mins): In small groups, students choose one element of U.S. pop culture (e.g., Hollywood films, hip-hop, Instagram influencers, fast food chains). Using AI, they investigate:<br>- How this element has spread globally<br>- How it influences cultural norms, language, fashion, or values in another country<br>- Whether this influence is seen as positive, negative, or complex<br>- How it connects to the idea of “soft power” (cultural influence as a form of power)<br><br>Example prompt for AI: “How has hip-hop culture influenced youth in South Korea?” or “What impact do American fast food brands have on local food culture in Vietnam?”<br>3. Mini Debate or Presentation (10 mins): Each group presents:<br>- Their chosen pop culture element<br>- Key insights from AI<br>- One example of cultural influence<br>- Their opinion: Is this cultural power empowering or problematic?<br>4. Individual Reflection (5 mins): Students write: “One way U.S. pop culture has influenced me is… I think it’s (positive/negative/mixed) because…”</p>\n<div class=\"ml-en\"><h3>Constructive questions — answer them yourself first</h3></div>\n<div class=\"ml-vi\"><h3>Câu hỏi kiến tạo — tự trả lời trước</h3></div>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>QN36.1</strong> — What have you learnt from your classmate's personal reflection?</li>\n<li><strong>QN36.2</strong> — What have you learnt from your classmate's personal reflection?</li>\n</ul>\n<div class=\"ml-en\"><div class=\"note-ct\">📝 Detailed lecture and 🎬 video for this session: coming later. For now follow the slides, the materials and the tasks above.</div></div>\n<div class=\"ml-vi\"><div class=\"note-ct\">📝 Bài giảng chi tiết và 🎬 video cho buổi này: sẽ bổ sung sau. Trước mắt học theo slide, tài liệu và nhiệm vụ ở trên.</div></div>"
